WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:04.920
Pete Davidson grew from an exceptionally&nbsp;
challenging childhood to an adult life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:11.160
marred by public scrutiny. From periods in rehab&nbsp;
to struggles with physical and mental disorders,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:14.800
these are the tragic details of Davidson's life.

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:19.160
Pete Davidson's early life was marred by&nbsp;
trauma in a way that few other people ever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:23.160
experience. When he was only 7 years&nbsp;
old, his father was killed during the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:27.480
September 11 attacks in New York. Scott&nbsp;
Matthew Davidson was a firefighter in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:31.360
city and was part of the response team&nbsp;
that attended the World Trade Center.

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:34.880
According to eyewitness accounts, Scott&nbsp;
was last seen running up the stairs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:39.560
of the Marriott World Trade Center hotel&nbsp;
moments before the Twin Towers collapsed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:43.800
completely destroying the building and&nbsp;
killing almost everyone who was inside.

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:48.120
Scott, who graduated from the fire&nbsp;
academy in 1994 before joining Ladder&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:53.600
Company 118 in Brooklyn Heights, had always&nbsp;
dreamed of being a firefighter. He was 33&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:57.440
years old at the time of his death. Pete&nbsp;
remembers him with a tattoo on his left&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:02.560
arm of his father's badge number alongside a&nbsp;
replica of the helmet he wore while on duty.

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:06.320
Scott's influence may well have been&nbsp;
a significant factor in Pete becoming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:11.720
a comedian as an adult. As an old schoolmate of&nbsp;
the fallen fighter recalled to the New York Post,

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:15.560
"Scott was always clowning around.&nbsp;
Telling jokes, making people laugh."

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:19.560
Despite the tragic nature of his father's&nbsp;
death, Davidson has dealt with the loss&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:24.480
with strength, even making jokes about&nbsp;
his father's passing when appropriate.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:27.440
Considering the traumatic loss of&nbsp;
his father, it's not surprising&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:30.760
that Davidson didn't have the perfect&nbsp;
childhood. The death of his father in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:34.200
such a shocking way was overwhelming&nbsp;
for the young boy, and his mother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:38.960
Amy Davidson, told the New York Times that&nbsp;
the future-comedian's upbringing was very sad.

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:41.640
According to the outlet, Davidson&nbsp;
attended three different high&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:45.440
schools due to conflicts with other&nbsp;
students and his own bad behavior.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:49.480
He even pulled out his own hair as&nbsp;
a result of his emotional turmoil.

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:54.200
He eventually came to realize that the problem&nbsp;
wasn't other kids — it was him. Speaking on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:58.560
Peacock's talk show Hart to Heart, Davidson&nbsp;
explained that it wasn't just his father's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:03.160
death that negatively affected his childhood. The&nbsp;
fact that his mother was a single parent and he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:09.640
had a very young sister also had an effect on him&nbsp;
despite his family being loving and supportive.

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:15.600
“Single mom, like, new sister. Just&nbsp;
like, did not handle it great."

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:20.840
It may seem odd, but Pete Davidson credits&nbsp;
Kid Cudi with saving his life as a child. His&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:25.480
mental health issues led to the youngster having&nbsp;
suicidal thoughts, and the comedian has since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:30.400
admitted that he believes that he may well have&nbsp;
ended his own life if it wasn't for the rapper&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:36.120
and singer. In particular, Davidson says that&nbsp;
the 2009 album Man on the Moon: The End of Day&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:42.240
saved his life. He confirmed this in an interview&nbsp;
with Power 105.1's The Breakfast Club, saying,

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:46.760
"I would've killed myself. Absolutely.&nbsp;
100 percent. I truly believe if Man on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:49.680
the Moon didn't come out, I wouldn't be here."

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:54.400
The comedian said the emotional nature of Kid&nbsp;
Cudi's music struck a chord with him and many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:59.240
other young people. In recent years, Kid Cudi has&nbsp;
spoken out about his own mental health problems,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:04.000
with the musician entering rehab&nbsp;
for depression in 2016. As an adult,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:07.920
Davidson has even gotten to work with&nbsp;
his idol, and he continues to appreciate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:12.880
that Kid Cudi was willing to speak so&nbsp;
openly about his personal experiences.

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:17.280
Davidson was first diagnosed with Crohn's&nbsp;
disease when he was still a teenager. Crohn's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:21.120
disease is a condition where parts of&nbsp;
the digestive system become inflamed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:26.520
causing a variety of painful symptoms, such&nbsp;
as diarrhea, stomach cramps, and fatigue.

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:29.280
Once diagnosed, Crohn's disease is not curable;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:33.800
patients live with it for the rest of their&nbsp;
lives. However, available treatments can help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:38.360
manage symptoms and allow those living with&nbsp;
the disease to live relatively normal lives.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:42.520
Treatments include medicines to help&nbsp;
alleviate symptoms and also surgery to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:48.040
remove small parts of the digestive system that&nbsp;
become particularly inflamed during flare-ups.

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:52.600
The unpredictable nature of the condition means&nbsp;
that it can be challenging to live with as it is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:57.360
impossible to know exactly when the symptoms&nbsp;
will occur. Davidson has been open about how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.360 --> 00:04:01.400
the condition affects him, telling High Times&nbsp;
that the disease would cause him so much pain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:07.640
he couldn't eat. However, he found that smoking&nbsp;
cannabis proved a reliable solution to this issue.

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:09.960
"Then I'd smoke and I'd be able&nbsp;
to eat and be able to do my shows,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.960 --> 00:04:12.080
and I wouldn't be able to do&nbsp;
SNL if I didn't smoke weed."

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:16.320
Davidson has also spoken openly about&nbsp;
having borderline personality disorder.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:19.200
This is a condition that affects&nbsp;
a person's thoughts and emotions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:22.240
as well as their ability to&nbsp;
communicate with other people.

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:26.320
Those living with the condition will often&nbsp;
act in a rash manner without considering the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:31.480
consequences and also have trouble controlling&nbsp;
their emotions. Exactly what causes borderline&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:36.080
personality disorder is unclear, although&nbsp;
it has been linked with traumatic events.

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:40.160
Davidson first revealed the diagnosis&nbsp;
during the film King of Staten Island,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:44.400
and has often talked about how he struggles&nbsp;
with regular bouts of depression. He later&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:49.360
said on the WTF With Marc Maron podcast that he&nbsp;
would have, quote, "mental breakdowns" where he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:54.040
would spiral into a rage and not remember.&nbsp;
To spread awareness about mental health,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:58.560
the comedian spoke up during a feature on SNL's&nbsp;
"Weekend Update" segment, urging viewers who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:04.480
may be suffering with depression or similar&nbsp;
conditions to talk to doctors and seek help.

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:06.360
"First of all, if you think you're depressed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:11.640
you know, see a doctor and talk to them&nbsp;
about medication and also be healthy."

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:15.720
The former SNL star has regularly checked&nbsp;
into rehabilitation facilities to help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:19.760
address his mental health. Most recently,&nbsp;
he entered a rehab center in Pennsylvania&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:24.160
in 2023 for in-patient therapy as a&nbsp;
result of his borderline personality&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:29.760
disorder and post-traumatic stress syndrome. As&nbsp;
a source close to Davidson confirmed to People,

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:34.040
"Pete will often check himself into&nbsp;
rehab to work on these issues."

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:37.920
As someone who has not been afraid to share&nbsp;
sensitive details of his personal life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:42.560
it is not particularly surprising that Pete&nbsp;
Davidson has been open about his addictions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:47.400
As a way of self-medicating, Davidson frequently&nbsp;
smokes cannabis and spent two stints in rehab&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:52.240
facilities trying to deal with his use of the&nbsp;
drug after blaming it for intense mood swings.

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:56.080
Over the course of his career, Davidson&nbsp;
has spent time in and out of rehab,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.080 --> 00:06:02.320
even spending a period completely free of drugs&nbsp;
and alcohol. As he wrote in a 2017 Instagram post,

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:07.000
"I quit drugs and am happy and sober for&nbsp;
the first time in 8 years. It wasn't easy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:11.280
but I got a great girl, great friends&nbsp;
and I consider myself a lucky man."

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:16.160
However, his sobriety didn't last long, and a&nbsp;
year later he was smoking and drinking again.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:20.200
Cannabis is not the only drug that has landed&nbsp;
him in rehab, either. According to People,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:24.360
during a comedy show with John Mulaney&nbsp;
and Jon Stewart in September 2023,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:27.160
he revealed that he had been&nbsp;
taking ketamine every day for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:32.360
four years before going to a rehabilitation&nbsp;
facility. He even joked to the audience,

00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:36.520
"I got that post-rehab glow.&nbsp;
Seventh time's the charm!"

00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:40.560
Like many other edgy comedians, Davidson&nbsp;
is no stranger to controversy and has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:45.480
often faced criticism for many of his&nbsp;
jokes. During an SNL sketch in 2019,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:50.120
he compared the Catholic Church to musician R.&nbsp;
Kelly after the latter had been convicted for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:55.120
crimes relating to child sex abuse. The year&nbsp;
prior, the Roman Catholic Diocese of Brooklyn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:59.640
had agreed to pay millions to settle a&nbsp;
lawsuit alleging sexual misconduct. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:04.520
same diocese demanded an apology from the&nbsp;
show and Davidson in response to the joke.

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:07.680
His Netflix special, Pete Davidson&nbsp;
Presents: Alive From New York,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.680 --> 00:07:12.080
also drew condemnation from many people within&nbsp;
the gay community for what were perceived to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:16.280
be homophobic jokes. More recently, the&nbsp;
Netflix special Pete Davidson Presents:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.280 --> 00:07:21.400
The Best Friends also caused controversy for&nbsp;
jokes referencing AIDS and Jeffrey Epstein.

00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:23.760
The comedian also famously apologized to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:28.134
Republican politician Dan Crenshaw&nbsp;
for mocking the eye patch he wears.

00:07:28.134 --> 00:07:32.640
"You may be surprised he's a&nbsp;
congressional candidate from Texas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:36.080
and not a hitman in a porno movie."

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:39.880
Sadly, Crenshaw wears the eyepatch as a&nbsp;
result of an injury he received while on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.880 --> 00:07:46.280
active duty in Afghanistan. Even so, Davidson&nbsp;
later retracted his apology to the politician.

00:07:46.280 --> 00:07:51.320
In 2018, Davidson caused concern when he&nbsp;
posted a cryptic message on Instagram.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:56.240
In the wake of his public split with his&nbsp;
ex-fiancée Ariana Grande, Davidson wrote,

00:07:56.240 --> 00:07:58.840
"I'm trying to understand how&nbsp;
when something happens to a guy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.840 --> 00:08:03.600
the whole entire world just trashes him&nbsp;
without any facts or frame of reference."

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:06.480
He also complained that he had&nbsp;
been bullied for nine months,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:10.320
seemingly in reference to his relationship&nbsp;
with the musician. Several days later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:14.280
police performed a welfare check after&nbsp;
Davidson again posted on Instagram,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:17.680
this time with a message suggesting&nbsp;
he was having suicidal thoughts.

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:20.720
He later deleted his social&nbsp;
media accounts altogether,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:25.440
further distressing fans. However, he did&nbsp;
continue to appear on Saturday Night Live,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:30.000
though neither he nor NBC have issued a&nbsp;
statement regarding the posts he made.

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:33.880
With Kim Kardashian being one of the&nbsp;
most well-known people on the planet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.880 --> 00:08:38.320
the fact that she was dating Pete Davidson&nbsp;
made headlines around the world. This news&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.320 --> 00:08:42.200
was further heightened due to her recent&nbsp;
split with her ex-husband Kanye West,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:44.920
who was seemingly unhappy with&nbsp;
the pair seeing each other.

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:49.880
In February 2022, West launched a tirade&nbsp;
against Davidson and even encouraged fans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:53.560
to verbally harass him in public.&nbsp;
The musician was later banned from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.560 --> 00:08:57.320
Instagram for 24 hours after making&nbsp;
threatening remarks to both Davidson&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.320 --> 00:09:01.520
and fellow comedian Trevor Noah. West&nbsp;
continued to post about Davidson and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:06.280
his relationship with Kim Kardashian months&nbsp;
later, even after the pair eventually split.

00:09:06.280 --> 00:09:11.000
The negative attention and threats from West&nbsp;
took a toll on Davidson. In August 2022,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:14.240
it was revealed that the comedian was&nbsp;
in trauma therapy as a result of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:17.000
interactions with West. As a source told People,

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:20.080
"The attention and negativity&nbsp;
coming from Kanye and his antics&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:23.240
is a trigger for [Pete], and&nbsp;
he's had to seek out help."

00:09:23.240 --> 00:09:26.600
Although they were no longer together,&nbsp;
Kardashian was supportive of Davidson&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.600 --> 00:09:31.520
seeking therapy and criticized&nbsp;
the behavior of her ex-husband.

00:09:31.520 --> 00:09:34.720
Davidson was one of the youngest&nbsp;
ever cast members to join SNL,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:38.000
first appearing on the show when&nbsp;
he was just 20 years old. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:41.840
that doesn't mean that the experience has&nbsp;
always been enjoyable. While he's said he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.840 --> 00:09:45.960
is thankful for the opportunities it has&nbsp;
given him, Davidson has also spoken out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:50.920
about how he feels he has been poorly treated&nbsp;
at times by his fellow writers and comedians.

00:09:50.920 --> 00:09:55.760
Speaking to Charlamagne Tha God, Davidson revealed&nbsp;
that he doesn't feel like the show has his back,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.760 --> 00:09:59.440
despite having a strong relationship&nbsp;
with executive producer Lorne Michaels.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.440 --> 00:10:02.760
Davidson believed that when he wasn't&nbsp;
around, his colleagues and castmates&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.760 --> 00:10:07.440
would talk poorly of him behind his back,&nbsp;
which upset and confused the rising star.

00:10:07.440 --> 00:10:11.680
On Jon Bernthal's Real Ones podcast,&nbsp;
Davidson went into more detail about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.680 --> 00:10:15.400
how jokes about his personal life made&nbsp;
working on the show more difficult. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:19.120
explained that there were moments on the show&nbsp;
where a joke would be made at his expense,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:22.880
and then he'd need to walk onstage to&nbsp;
the derisive laughter of the audience.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.880 --> 00:10:27.920
He stated that, over time, that began&nbsp;
to take a toll on his own self-image.

00:10:27.920 --> 00:10:30.800
"You know, because it seems like&nbsp;
all really talented people are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.800 --> 00:10:35.000
sick. Don't worry Colin, me and you are good."

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:37.960
Anyone who is familiar with Pete&nbsp;
Davidson will know that he has an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.960 --> 00:10:42.160
extensive number of tattoos across his&nbsp;
entire body. These range from references&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:46.440
to previous girlfriends to designs by his&nbsp;
friends like Machine Gun Kelly to pieces he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.440 --> 00:10:50.840
purposefully got while filming a role. The&nbsp;
comedian even has a matching tattoo with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.840 --> 00:10:55.360
Miley Cyrus as the two appeared in an SNL&nbsp;
sketch together where they played babies.

00:10:55.360 --> 00:10:59.600
Davidson has, in recent years, begun to&nbsp;
have many of these tattoos removed. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:03.000
explained on Late Night with Seth Meyers&nbsp;
that this was a decision he made because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:06.840
of his career in Hollywood. It takes&nbsp;
so long to cover up the tattoos when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.840 --> 00:11:10.760
filming that it made more sense for the&nbsp;
comedian to get rid of them completely.

00:11:10.760 --> 00:11:15.000
What many people may not realize, though, is that&nbsp;
one of the reasons that Davidson started getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:20.080
tattoos in the first place was to cover up scars&nbsp;
from self-harm. Speaking with Charlamagne tha God,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.080 --> 00:11:23.800
Davidson noted that some of the tattoos on&nbsp;
his chest specifically are there to hide&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.800 --> 00:11:27.480
scars from cutting himself there.&nbsp;
He also revealed that, at times,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.480 --> 00:11:31.680
he saw self-harm as his only option&nbsp;
for a release while stressed, saying,

00:11:31.680 --> 00:11:36.240
"Whenever you're so manic and upset, sometimes&nbsp;
that's the only thing that will work for me."

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:39.920
Thankfully, Davidson's stints in rehab&nbsp;
have exposed him to healthier coping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:39.920 --> 00:11:44.120
mechanisms in situations where&nbsp;
he feels emotionally overwhelmed.

